ust for power  so it's interesting to hear from some  lower level villains  in chapter 15 the believer mando has to  sneak into an imperial base with former  imperial sharpshooter  mix mayfield and before the pair can  sneak back out  they're cornered by hess he was once  mayfield's superior officer  when mayfield asked hess how he could  sacrifice his entire division to wipe  out a city  hess replies see boys everybody thinks  they want freedom  but what they really want is order  hes toasty empire at which point  mayfield shoots him dead  but before that hess's monologue offers  a rare glimpse into the mindset  of the empire's military commanders and  it's chilling  even though his answer doesn't come as a  surprise given that the mandalorian  focuses on characters who have reasons  for avoiding the new republic  after the fall of the empire it's  unsurprising that we don't see many  former rebels  pilate carson tiva and his wingman  trapper wolf are exceptions  along with others from the rebel ranks  who helps take down the empire the pair  now monitors goings-on in an official  capacity  policing a galaxy healing after decades  of strife mandalorian viewers are  introduced to the duo in chapter 10 the  passenger when mando's attempt to avoid  them nearly gets him eaten by a giant  space spider  it isn't just that he's feeling shy  after teaver and wolf rescue him  we find out there's a warrant out for  his arrest when bando asks teva if he's  going to try and take him into custody  the pilot admits he or two but for  better or worse the new republic is far  from the authoritarian regime that the  empire was  and tiva lets him go this encounter is  more than a glimpse of republic police  work in action  the mandalorian also threw in a fun  easter egg for fans to discover longtime  star wars writer and mandalorian  producer  occasional director dave felloni plays  trapper wolf  and with the upcoming star wars disney  plus series rangers of the new republic  which 